I've been toying with the idea of making a middle/late game
gameplay patch, that falls somewhere between "Gehennom
is boring", and "next version wishlist."  I've tried to keep
the ideas limited to things simple enough for me to code; a
tough standard.[1]

Anyway, here are some of the more specific ideas.

* HP/SP cap
The cap would be a bit soft. HP/SP max over the cap would drift
down towards it at a speed proportional to your healing rate. But
slow enough where someone could enjoy having huge HP for awhile
if they really wanted to. Race and class big inputs to the cap.

* Diminishing returns on negative AC.
Leaning towards: DR = min(min(rnd(-ac),rnd(-ac)),20).

* Nerfed Reflection
Instead of each reflection-giving item granting perfect reflection,
items would have individual probabilities of reflecting attacks, and
each item gets a chance to reflect any one attack. Rough shot at
numbers: artifacts (generally) 90%, AoR 95%, SDSM 99%, SoR 99.9%,
being-a-SD 100%. Breath weapons harder to reflect.

* But wait, Gehennom is still boring
Here's what I'm thinking about doing to Gehennom:
- Make the mazes generally more open, with more monsters initially.
- Shorten it from top to bottom.
- Move all the lairs out to side branches. Lair chosen randomly
  to have Candelabrum. Other lairs have goodies.
- Bonuses for demons and demon princes. HP, speed, resistances,
  Elbereth-immunity.

* Some small tweaks, like speed boosts for dragons.

